From: Razer Edge port draft
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: snps-femto-v2: hand the datapath back in device mode

On the Razer Edge (SM8350) with the Type-C graph in place (pmic_glink altmode
enabled) the ADSP's charger detection takes DP/DM over on every sink attach:
about 11 ms after the partner shows up, USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_CFG0 has
UTMI_PHY_DATAPATH_CTRL_OVERRIDE_EN set and UTMI_CTRL0 OPMODE is non-driving.
Nothing in Linux writes either. The host resets the bus, the gadget stays in
"default" and the link suspends. The downstream kernel re-initialises the PHY
on every attach and never notices; mainline initialises it once.

Clear both when peripheral mode is set on an initialised PHY. The host
re-enumerates on its own once they are clear (seen: "configured" within a
few seconds, no gadget re-bind). ucsi_glink calls this after a sink attach.

Found on the Razer Edge (31 Ekim 2026) with a 10 ms register watch.
---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
index 980ad1fb1..adf8d81b5 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
@@ -232,6 +232,20 @@ static int qcom_snps_hsphy_set_mode(struct phy *phy, enum phy_mode mode,
 	struct qcom_snps_hsphy *hsphy = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
 
 	hsphy->mode = mode;
+
+	/*
+	 * Charger detection in the ADSP (seen on SM8350) takes DP/DM over on
+	 * every attach and leaves the PHY non-driving with the UTMI datapath
+	 * overridden: the host resets the bus and enumeration stalls. Hand the
+	 * datapath back to the controller when peripheral mode is asked for.
+	 */
+	if (mode == PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE && hsphy->phy_initialized) {
+		qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base, USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_UTMI_CTRL0,
+					   OPMODE_MASK, OPMODE_NORMAL);
+		qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base, USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_CFG0,
+					   UTMI_PHY_DATAPATH_CTRL_OVERRIDE_EN, 0);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
